  "text": {
    "intro": "Down the board, judged on the floor as much as on the clock, and the wool classer is taking notes.\nFive shearers are involved. Determine each shearer's placing, handpiece and penalty.\n- **Shearer**: Rangi, Manaia, Deirdre Pollok, Tipene and Bevan Toft.\n- **Placing** (listed from better to worse): first, second, third, fourth and fifth.\n- **Handpiece**: a spare set of blades, a wide comb, a borrowed handpiece, Lister blades and an old Sunbeam.\n- **Penalty**: a missed belly, tufts on the britch, a slow pen, a skin nick and a faultless board.\nEvery shearer has a different placing, handpiece and penalty, so within each category every item is used exactly once.",
    "clues": [
      "Tipene places third.",
      "Third is exactly one place better than the shearer who uses an old Sunbeam, with no placing in between.",
      "The shearer who is docked for a faultless board and fourth are exactly one place apart in placing order, in one direction or the other.",
      "The shearer who uses Lister blades and Manaia both sit at odd-numbered places or both at even-numbered places. Manaia is better than fourth in placing order.",
      "The shearer who uses a borrowed handpiece is better than fifth in placing order.",
      "The shearer who is docked for a skin nick falls somewhere between the shearer who uses a wide comb and Deirdre Pollok in placing order.",
      "The shearer who uses Lister blades and Deirdre Pollok are exactly two places apart in placing order.",
      "Tipene is exactly one place better than the shearer who is docked for a skin nick, with no placing in between.",
      "The shearer who is docked for tufts on the britch and Bevan Toft are exactly three places apart in placing order.",
      "The shearer who uses a wide comb and the shearer who is docked for a missed belly are exactly two places apart in placing order."
